\ Spitfire: the aircraft's models, each a sketch in its own terms, metres
\ right, up and forward of its centre, its faces filled and its edges kept
\ for the briefing's wireframe: bodies as rings along their length, flat
\ surfaces on both sides with their hinge lines, fins, propellers; and the
\ Spitfire Mk I and the Hurricane Mk I, wheels up or down.
\
\ The Spitfire is built to its published span and length (11.23 m,
\ 9.12 m), wing area (22.48 m², as in flight.telic) and dihedral (6°). Its
\ wing is an ellipse: a chord at each distance out of the root chord times
\ √(1 − (out ÷ half-span)²), the root chord 2.55 m being what an ellipse of
\ that span and area has, the leading edge 30% of the chord ahead of a
\ straight spar line and the trailing edge 70% behind it. Every other
\ figure is an estimate from drawings: the fuselage's rings, the hood, the
\ tail surfaces, the radiator under the starboard wing and the oil cooler
\ under the port, the propeller's 1.64 m radius, the undercarriage's track.

\ one ring of a body, points about its centre line: the ring is [ along half-width half-height lift ], the centre where the line runs
: body-ring ( ring centre n-sides -- points )
	| ring centre n-sides |
	ring spread to lift to half-height to half-width to along
	[ 0 n-sides 1 do k
		k n-sides / TAU * to angle
		centre [ angle sin half-width * angle cos half-height * lift + along ] v+
	loop ] ;

\ the ring of a body of rings at a station along, between the two rings around it in proportion
: body-ring-at ( rings along -- ring )
	| rings along |
	0 rings size 1- 1 do k
		rings k @i to front
		rings k 1+ @i to back
		along front first <= along back first >= and if
			back front along back first - front first back first - / v-between to ring
		then
	loop
	ring ;

\ a point on the upper shoulder of a body of rings about the line through the origin, the rings' corners 45° up a side, -1 the left and 1 the right: where the skin between the two rings around a station along passes the station
: body-shoulder ( rings along side -- point )
	| rings along side |
	rings along body-ring-at spread to lift to half-height to half-width drop
	[ side half-width * 0.5 sqrt * half-height 0.5 sqrt * lift + along ] ;

\ the height of the top of a body of rings about the line through the origin at a station along
: body-top ( rings along -- height )
	| rings along |
	rings along body-ring-at to ring
	ring 2 @i ring 3 @i + ;

\ a point on a side of a body of rings about the line through the origin, at a station along and a height between the shoulders 45° above and below the side's ridge: on the skin's face between the ridge and the nearer shoulder, a distance proud of it across
: body-side-point ( rings along up side proud -- point )
	| rings along up side proud |
	rings along body-ring-at spread to lift to half-height to half-width drop
	up lift - abs half-height 0.5 sqrt * / to rise
	[ side half-width 1 1 0.5 sqrt - rise * - * proud + * up along ] ;

\ a body as rings along its length, joined ring to ring, its skin filled between them and its ends closed: a fuselage, a nacelle
: sketch-body ( sketch rings centre n-sides -- )
	| sketch rings centre n-sides |
	rings ( ring | sketch ring centre n-sides body-ring sketch-points ) map to ring-indices
	rings ( ring | centre [ 0 ring 3 @i ring first ] v+ ) map to axis
	ring-indices ( indices | sketch indices join-loop ) each
	0 ring-indices size 1- 1 do k
		ring-indices k @i to front
		ring-indices k 1+ @i to back
		axis k @i axis k 1+ @i 0.5 v-between to inside
		0 n-sides 1 do corner
			corner 1+ n-sides mod to next
			sketch front corner @i back corner @i sketch-edge
			sketch [ front corner @i front next @i back next @i back corner @i ] inside sketch-face
		loop
	loop
	sketch ring-indices first axis second sketch-face
	sketch ring-indices last axis axis size 2 - @i sketch-face ;

\ a box centred on a point rather than standing on it
: sketch-box-centred ( sketch centre heading width length height -- )
	| sketch centre heading width length height |
	sketch centre [ 0 height 2 / negate 0 ] v+ heading width length height sketch-box ;

\ [ out along ] points of a surface's right half, on the side given, rising by a slope from a height
: surface-points ( outline side slope height -- points )
	| outline side slope height |
	outline ( pair | [ pair first side * pair first slope * height + pair second ] ) map ;

\ a flat surface on both sides, wings or tailplanes: its outline closed and filled, and its hinge lines
: sketch-surface ( sketch outline hinges slope height -- )
	| sketch outline hinges slope height |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch outline side slope height surface-points null sketch-plate
		hinges ( hinge | sketch hinge side slope height surface-points sketch-path ) each
	) each ;

\ a fin a distance out from the centre line: its outline filled and its rudder's hinge, as [ along up ] points
: sketch-fin ( sketch out outline hinge -- )
	| sketch out outline hinge |
	sketch outline ( pair | [ out pair second pair first ] ) map null sketch-plate
	sketch hinge ( pair | [ out pair second pair first ] ) map sketch-path ;

\ a propeller: three blades of a radius from the hub
: sketch-propeller ( sketch hub radius -- )
	| sketch hub radius |
	0 3 1 do k
		k 3 / TAU * 0.35 + to angle
		sketch [ hub hub [ angle sin radius * angle cos radius * 0 ] v+ ] sketch-path
	loop ;

\ a circle of points about a centre in the plane of two directions
: ring-of ( centre across up radius n-points -- points )
	| centre across up radius n-points |
	[ 0 n-points 1 do k
		k n-points / TAU * to angle
		centre across angle cos radius * v* v+ up angle sin radius * v* v+
	loop ] ;

: sketch-ring ( sketch centre across up radius n-points -- )
	| sketch centre across up radius n-points |
	sketch centre across up radius n-points ring-of sketch-loop ;

\ painted discs on a surface, one inside the next, each a little farther out along the surface's outward direction so it lies over the one before; the radii from the largest, a colour for each
: sketch-roundel ( sketch centre across up outward radii colours -- )
	| sketch centre across up outward radii colours |
	0 radii size 1 do k
		centre outward k 1+ 0.004 * v* v+ to lifted
		sketch lifted across up radii k @i 16 ring-of lifted outward v- colours k @i sketch-painted-plate
	loop ;

\ the spinners as rings from their points back to the cowling
: spitfire-spinner-rings ( -- rings ) [ [ 4.05 0.02 0.02 0 ] [ 3.85 0.22 0.22 0 ] [ 3.45 0.33 0.33 0 ] ] ;
: hurricane-spinner-rings ( -- rings ) [ [ 3.3 0.02 0.02 0.05 ] [ 3.1 0.18 0.18 0.05 ] [ 2.85 0.28 0.28 0.05 ] ] ;

\ the propellers' hubs, and their blades' half widths at the root and at the tip, metres
spitfire-mk-i-figures :hub @ constant spitfire-hub
hurricane-mk-i-figures :hub @ constant hurricane-hub
[ 0.09 0.05 ] constant spitfire-blade-widths
[ 0.1 0.06 ] constant hurricane-blade-widths

\ one blade of a three-blade propeller of 1.64 m radius as a closed outline: from 0.3 m out at the root to the tip, half widths given, turned an angle from straight up, clockwise seen from behind
: propeller-blade ( hub angle widths -- points )
	| hub angle widths |
	[ angle cos angle sin negate 0 ] to across
	[ angle sin angle cos 0 ] to outward
	widths spread to tip-half to root-half
	[ hub outward 0.3 v* v+ across root-half v* v+  hub outward 1.64 v* v+ across tip-half v* v+
	  hub outward 1.64 v* v+ across tip-half negate v* v+  hub outward 0.3 v* v+ across root-half negate v* v+ ] ;

\ a propeller's disc as the turning blades show it: a ring of their radius about the hub, square to the line of flight
: sketch-propeller-disc ( sketch hub radius -- )
	| sketch hub radius |
	sketch hub [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] radius 48 sketch-ring ;

\ the tyres' black (an estimate)
0x262626 constant tyre-colour

\ a simple aircraft: a four-sided body along its length, the wings', the tailplane's and the fin's outlines filled, a line for each engine out on the wing; in its upper colour, the faces turned down in its under colour
: far-model ( span length engine-out colour under-colour -- model )
	| span length engine-out colour under-colour |
	new-model-sketch to model
	model under-colour :under-colour ! to model
	length 2 / to half-length
	model [ [ half-length 0.1 0.1 0 ] [ half-length 0.4 * length 0.05 * length 0.06 * 0 ] [ half-length -1 * 0.05 0.05 0.2 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 4 sketch-body
	span 2 / to half-span
	length 0.14 * to chord
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		model [ [ 0 0 chord ] [ half-span side * span 0.03 * chord 0.3 * ] [ half-span side * span 0.03 * chord -0.4 * ] [ 0 0 chord -1 * ] ] null sketch-plate
		model [ [ 0 0.1 half-length -0.8 * ] [ span 0.12 * side * 0.1 half-length -0.9 * ] [ span 0.12 * side * 0.1 half-length -1 * ] [ 0 0.1 half-length -1 * ] ] null sketch-plate
		engine-out 0 > if model [ [ engine-out side * 0 chord 1.2 * ] [ engine-out side * 0 chord -1.5 * ] ] sketch-path then
	) each
	model [ [ 0 0.1 half-length -0.75 * ] [ 0 length 0.18 * half-length -0.95 * ] [ 0 length 0.18 * half-length -1 * ] [ 0 0.1 half-length -1 * ] ] null sketch-plate
	model colour sketch>object ;

\ === the finish of 1940 ===

\ the upper surfaces' colours (BS 381C: 641 Dark Green, 450 Dark Earth, 636 PRU Blue, 210 Sky, as w3schools' British Standard table renders them), and the roundel's red, blue and white (estimates of the dull wartime shades)
0x484837 constant dark-green-colour
0x745f46 constant dark-earth-colour
0x5f7682 constant pru-blue-colour
0xbbc9a5 constant sky-paint-colour
0x2c3768 constant roundel-blue-colour
0x8a2a26 constant roundel-red-colour
0xd8d8d0 constant roundel-white-colour

\ the Type B roundel on each upper wing, red and blue: the Spitfire's 55 in across with a 22 in red centre (Hooton, 1982), the Hurricane's 49 in (a modeller's reference for a Hurricane of August 1940) with its centre in the same proportion
55 0.0254 * 2 / constant spitfire-roundel-radius
22 0.0254 * 2 / constant spitfire-roundel-centre-radius
49 0.0254 * 2 / constant hurricane-roundel-radius
hurricane-roundel-radius 22 55 / * constant hurricane-roundel-centre-radius

\ the Dark Earth on the upper wings in the Temperate Land Scheme's A pattern, which the Air Ministry's drawings set out for the single-engine monoplanes from 1937 and the factories applied to every other aircraft (the B pattern its mirror image), the rest Dark Green: closed outlines of [ out share ] points, the distance out to the right (to the left negative) and the share of the chord back from the leading edge, traced at 5 cm and 2% of the chord from the plan views of TopNotch's 1940 pattern A mask sets for the Spitfire Mk I to V and the Hurricane Mk I and II, which follow those drawings; outlines reach a little past the edges, which cut them, and the Hurricane's one patch of green inside the brown ahead of the left roundel, 5 dm², is left brown
