\ the Dark Earth patches laid 15 mm over the upper wings' skin, each painted on its upper side only: each patch cut to the chord, and to each wing between the fuselage's side, a distance out, and the tip, so a patch across the fuselage becomes two; each corner [ out share ] placed on the skin by a word
: sketch-dark-earth ( sketch patches root tip skin -- )
	| sketch patches root tip skin |
	[ [ root 1 tip -1 ] [ root negate -1 tip negate 1 ] ] to wings
	0 patches size 1 do p
		patches p @i 1 0 1 clip-pairs 1 1 -1 clip-pairs to cut
		0 2 1 do w
			wings w @i spread to tip-keep to tip-limit to root-keep to root-limit
			cut 0 root-limit root-keep clip-pairs 0 tip-limit tip-keep clip-pairs to piece
			piece size 3 >= if
				[ 0 piece size 1 do c piece c @i spread skin execute [ 0 0.015 0 ] v+ loop ] to corners
				corners [ 0 0 0 ] ' v+ reduce 1 corners size / v* [ 0 1 0 ] v- to below
				sketch corners below dark-earth-colour sketch-painted-plate
			then
		loop
	loop ;

\ === the Spitfire ===

\ the elliptical surfaces' chord at a distance out
: elliptical-chord ( out half-span root-chord -- chord )
	| out half-span root-chord |
	1 out half-span / sq - 0 max2 sqrt root-chord * ;

\ an elliptical surface's right half as [ out along ] points: the leading edge out through the stations to the tip, then the trailing edge back; the spar line at an along, the leading edge a share of the chord ahead of it
: elliptical-outline ( stations half-span root-chord spar lead -- pairs )
	| stations half-span root-chord spar lead |
	stations ( out | [ out out half-span root-chord elliptical-chord lead * spar + ] ) map to leading
	stations reverse ( out | [ out out half-span root-chord elliptical-chord 1 lead - * spar swap - ] ) map to trailing
	leading [ [ half-span spar ] ] concat trailing concat ;

\ a hinge line across an elliptical surface, a share of the chord ahead of the trailing edge, through stations
: elliptical-hinge ( stations half-span root-chord spar lead share -- pairs )
	| stations half-span root-chord spar lead share |
	stations ( out | [ out out half-span root-chord elliptical-chord 1 lead - share - * spar swap - ] ) map ;

5.615 constant spitfire-half-span
2.55 constant spitfire-root-chord
1.565 constant spitfire-spar
6 PI 180 / * tan constant spitfire-dihedral
-0.70 constant spitfire-wing-height

\ the wing's height above the centre line at a distance out
: wing-height-at ( out -- up ) abs spitfire-dihedral * spitfire-wing-height + ;

\ the wing's lower skin below its chord plane at the root, narrowing with the chord to the tip
0.15 constant spitfire-root-depth

\ the wing's underside at a distance out
: wing-underside-at ( out -- up )
	| out |
	out wing-height-at out abs spitfire-half-span spitfire-root-chord elliptical-chord spitfire-root-chord / spitfire-root-depth * - ;

\ the wing's leading and trailing edges at a distance out
: wing-leading-at ( out -- along ) abs spitfire-half-span spitfire-root-chord elliptical-chord 0.3 * spitfire-spar + ;
: wing-trailing-at ( out -- along ) abs spitfire-half-span spitfire-root-chord elliptical-chord 0.7 * spitfire-spar swap - ;

\ the point on the wing's chord plane a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge
: spitfire-skin ( out share -- point )
	| out share |
	out wing-leading-at to leading
	[ out out wing-height-at leading leading out wing-trailing-at - share * - ] ;

\ a NACA four-digit section's upper surface above its chord line at a share of the chord back from the leading edge, as a share of the chord: its camber line, the greatest camber a share of the chord at a place along it, and half its thickness, a share of the chord, over it
: naca-upper ( x camber place thickness -- up )
	| x camber place thickness |
	x sqrt 0.2969 * x 0.126 * - x sq 0.3516 * - x 3 ^ 0.2843 * + x 4 ^ 0.1015 * - thickness 5 * * to half-thickness
	x place < if
		camber place sq / place 2 * x * x sq - *
	else
		camber 1 place - sq / 1 place 2 * - place 2 * x * + x sq - *
	then half-thickness + ;

\ the wing's upper surface at a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge: the NACA 2213 section at the root thinning to 2209.4 at the tip (published), the 2% camber at 20% of the chord, over the chord plane
: spitfire-upper-at ( out fraction -- up )
	| out fraction |
	out abs spitfire-half-span / to share
	out abs spitfire-half-span spitfire-root-chord elliptical-chord to chord
	fraction 0 1 clamp 0.02 0.2 0.094 0.13 - share * 0.13 + naca-upper chord * out wing-height-at + ;

\ the aileron's ends' distances out, measured on the Mk Vb three-view on Wikimedia Commons, the Mk I's planform, at 119.3 pixels a metre, their 2.1 m span the published 6 ft 10½ in; its chord behind the hinge 0.42 m at its inner end as measured there, narrowing so its mean is the published area less the balance's over its length, 9.45 and 2.45 sq ft, 0.31 m; the split flap 8 ft 11 in a side, 2.72 m, ending at the aileron, its chord from its area, 15.6 sq ft for both, 0.27 m (Measurements of the Flying Qualities of a Supermarine Spitfire VA Airplane, NACA, 1942)
2.8 constant spitfire-aileron-inner
4.9 constant spitfire-aileron-outer
0.27 constant spitfire-flap-chord

\ the aileron's chord behind its hinge at a distance out
: spitfire-aileron-chord ( out -- chord ) spitfire-aileron-inner - spitfire-aileron-outer spitfire-aileron-inner - / 0.22 * 0.42 swap - ;

\ the right wing's outline, the split flap's hinge and the aileron's, as [ out along ] points
: spitfire-wing-outline ( -- pairs ) [ 0 1.5 2.5 3.5 4.3 4.9 5.3 5.5 5.6 ] spitfire-half-span spitfire-root-chord spitfire-spar 0.3 elliptical-outline ;
: spitfire-flap-hinge ( -- pairs ) [ 0.6 1.6 2.6 spitfire-aileron-inner ] ( out | [ out out wing-trailing-at spitfire-flap-chord + ] ) map ;
: spitfire-aileron-hinge ( -- pairs )
	[ spitfire-aileron-inner 3.5 4.2 spitfire-aileron-outer ] ( out | [ out out wing-trailing-at out spitfire-aileron-chord + ] ) map ;

\ the wings: the ellipse with its dihedral, the split flaps' and the ailerons' hinge lines and their ends, the four Browning ports in each leading edge
: sketch-spitfire-wings ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	spitfire-wing-outline to outline
	spitfire-flap-hinge to flap
	spitfire-aileron-hinge to aileron
	[ flap last aileron first aileron last ] ( hinge-end | [ [ hinge-end first hinge-end first wing-trailing-at ] hinge-end ] ) map to ends
	sketch outline [ flap aileron ] ends concat spitfire-dihedral spitfire-wing-height sketch-surface
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch outline ( pair | [ pair first side * pair first wing-underside-at pair second ] ) map null sketch-plate
	) each
	[ 1.9 2.15 2.9 3.15 ] ( out |
		[ -1 1 ] ( side |
			sketch [ [ out side * out wing-height-at out wing-leading-at ] [ out side * out wing-height-at out wing-leading-at 0.14 + ] ] sketch-path
		) each
	) each ;

\ the cockpit's three pieces: the raked windscreen, the blown sliding hood, the rear fixed windows
\ a cross-section of the blown sliding hood at a place along the fuselage, from the left lower edge over the top to the right: bulging well out past the lower edge at a third of its height, scaled across and to a height above a base, leaning from its along at the base to its along at the top
: hood-section ( base-along top-along across-scale height base -- points )
	| base-along top-along across-scale height base |
	[ [ -0.30 0 ] [ -0.40 0.08 ] [ -0.41 0.17 ] [ -0.33 0.27 ] [ -0.18 0.34 ] [ 0 0.36 ]
	  [ 0.18 0.34 ] [ 0.33 0.27 ] [ 0.41 0.17 ] [ 0.40 0.08 ] [ 0.30 0 ] ]
	( pair | pair second 0.36 / to share
		[ pair first across-scale * share height * base + top-along base-along - share * base-along + ] ) map ;

\ the Mk I's cockpit in three pieces: the windscreen, raked back from its base to its top on the hood's arc, its base sloping down to the hood's lower edge, a four-sided frame each side and the flat armoured panel between them; the blown sliding hood, drawn as its outline: the hoops at its front and rear, the arc along its top from the windscreen's top to its rear, its lower edge and sill line each side; the rear fixed window each side, a frame from the hood's rear edge back to the razorback spine with its glass inside, and the spine's top line (heights and positions measured on the Mk I side view at historyofwar.org/Pictures/pictures_spitfire_side.html, scaled to the published 9.12 m length)
\ the Spitfire's rear fixed windows, each side's frame and its glass inside it, closed outlines
: spitfire-rear-windows ( -- loops )
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ [ [ side 0.24 * 0.31 -0.11 ] [ side 0.18 * 0.59 -0.11 ] [ side 0.08 * 0.57 -0.6 ] [ side 0.24 * 0.31 -0.6 ] ]
		  [ [ side 0.235 * 0.37 -0.17 ] [ side 0.18 * 0.56 -0.17 ] [ side 0.09 * 0.55 -0.57 ] [ side 0.235 * 0.37 -0.57 ] ] ]
	) map [ ] ' concat reduce ;

: sketch-hood ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch [ [ side 0.24 * 0.36 0.89 ] [ side 0.18 * 0.60 0.60 ] [ side 0.18 * 0.61 0.49 ] [ side 0.26 * 0.28 0.36 ] ] sketch-loop
		sketch [ [ side 0.10 * 0.36 0.89 ] [ side 0.08 * 0.60 0.60 ] ] sketch-path
		sketch [ [ side 0.26 * 0.24 0.31 ] [ side 0.26 * 0.24 -0.11 ] ] sketch-path
		sketch [ [ side 0.29 * 0.29 0.31 ] [ side 0.29 * 0.29 -0.11 ] ] sketch-path
	) each
	spitfire-rear-windows ( window | sketch window sketch-loop ) each
	sketch [ [ -0.24 0.36 0.89 ] [ 0.24 0.36 0.89 ] ] sketch-path
	sketch [ [ -0.18 0.60 0.60 ] [ 0.18 0.60 0.60 ] ] sketch-path
	sketch [ [ 0 0.60 0.60 ] [ 0 0.61 0.49 ] [ 0 0.615 0.46 ] [ 0 0.626 0.42 ] [ 0 0.637 0.35 ] [ 0 0.637 0.21 ] [ 0 0.637 0.08 ]
	         [ 0 0.626 0.01 ] [ 0 0.615 -0.07 ] [ 0 0.60 -0.11 ] ] sketch-path
	sketch 0.31 0.42 0.85 0.386 0.24 hood-section sketch-path
	sketch -0.11 -0.11 0.85 0.36 0.24 hood-section sketch-path
	sketch [ [ 0 0.60 -0.11 ] [ 0 0.57 -0.65 ] ] sketch-path ;

\ the radiator under the starboard wing, one rectangular duct on the wing's underside with flat sides from the intake back to the exit: its frames at the intake, at the flap's hinge and at the exit, joined along the corners, and the hinge's line across the bottom, the flap behind it angled down to hold the exit open (along positions measured on the Mk I side view; the depths and the width estimates from photographs of the underside)
: sketch-radiator ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	1.55 wing-underside-at to top
	[ [ 1.36 0.27 ] [ 0.40 0.24 ] [ 0.18 0.29 ] ] ( station | station spread to depth to along
		[ [ 1.25 top along ] [ 1.85 top along ] [ 1.85 top depth - along ] [ 1.25 top depth - along ] ] ) map to frames
	frames ( frame | sketch frame sketch-points ) map to frame-indices
	sketch frame-indices first join-loop
	sketch frame-indices last join-loop
	[ 1.55 top 0.13 - 0.8 ] to inside
	0 4 1 do corner
		corner 1+ 4 mod to next
		sketch frame-indices ( indices | indices corner @i ) map join-path
		0 2 1 do k
			frame-indices k @i to front
			frame-indices k 1+ @i to back
			sketch [ front corner @i front next @i back next @i back corner @i ] inside sketch-face
		loop
	loop
	sketch [ frames second 2 @i frames second 3 @i ] sketch-path ;

\ the wheels' hubs, grey (an estimate)
0x8a8a86 constant hub-colour

\ a wheel rolling along the line of flight: its tyre's two faces a width apart along its axle, joined around the tread, all filled, and the hub, a share of the radius, on the face the axle points to; the axle and the wheel's up are unit vectors square to the line of flight
: sketch-wheel ( sketch centre axle up radius width hub-share -- )
	| sketch centre axle up radius width hub-share |
	[ -1 1 ] ( face | sketch centre axle face width * 2 / v* v+ [ 0 0 1 ] up radius 12 ring-of sketch-points ) map to rims
	rims ( rim | sketch rim join-loop sketch rim centre tyre-colour sketch-painted-face ) each
	0 12 1 do k
		k 1+ 12 mod to next
		sketch rims first k @i rims second k @i sketch-edge
		sketch [ rims first k @i rims first next @i rims second next @i rims second k @i ] centre tyre-colour sketch-painted-face
	loop
	centre axle width 2 / 0.005 + v* v+ to hub
	sketch hub [ 0 0 1 ] up radius hub-share * 12 ring-of centre hub-colour sketch-painted-plate ;

\ the undercarriage, down, as it swings out from the fuselage to retract: each leg a slim strut from its pivot near the fuselage down, out and forward, raked 18°, leaning 15° outward to the wheel's inner face 0.75 m below the pivot, with a short link near its foot; the wheel upright, for a track of 5 ft 8 in, its tyre a third of its diameter wide, its hub on the outer face; the leg's cover inboard of the wheel, a half-disc over the tyre's upper half, its edge an arc about the hub and straight across at the hub's height; the tailwheel and its leg (the track and the rake from a forum thread on the Mk Vb's undercarriage; the pivots, the leg's length, the cover and the tyre estimates from photographs)
: sketch-undercarriage ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ side 0.559 * -0.77 1.565 ] to pivot
		spitfire-mk-i-figures :main-wheel @ spread to wheel-along to wheel-up to wheel-out
		[ side wheel-out * wheel-up wheel-along ] to centre
		[ side 0 0 ] to axle
		[ 0 1 0 ] to up
		centre axle -0.105 v* v+ to foot
		[ -1 1 ] ( edge | sketch [ pivot [ 0 0 edge 0.04 * ] v+ foot [ 0 0 edge 0.04 * ] v+ ] sketch-path ) each
		sketch [ foot up 0.25 v* v+ [ 0 0 -0.12 ] v+ foot up 0.12 v* v+ [ 0 0 -0.16 ] v+ foot [ 0 0 -0.06 ] v+ ] sketch-path
		centre axle -0.135 v* v+ to cover-centre
		[ 0 9 1 do k
			k 8 / PI * to angle
			cover-centre up angle sin 0.37 * v* v+ [ 0 0 angle cos 0.37 * ] v+
		loop ] to arc
		sketch arc null sketch-plate
		sketch centre axle up spitfire-mk-i-figures :wheel-radius @ 0.21 0.3 sketch-wheel
	) each
	spitfire-mk-i-figures :tail-wheel @ to tail-wheel
	sketch [ [ 0 -0.35 -4.3 ] tail-wheel ] sketch-path
	sketch tail-wheel [ 0 0 1 ] [ 0 1 0 ] spitfire-mk-i-figures :tail-wheel-radius @ 8 ring-of tyre-colour sketch-plate ;

\ the Spitfire Mk I: the fuselage of eight-sided rings from the cowling to the tail, its profile measured on the same side view as the hood, the cowling's top level with the spinner's and its bottom curving down behind it, the spinner and the three-blade propeller, six exhaust stubs a side, the hood, the wings, the radiator and the oil cooler, the elliptical tailplane and elevators, the fin and rudder, the aerial mast, the roundels on the upper wings and the fuselage; the undercarriage when down. Filled in Dark Green with the Dark Earth patches on the upper wings, the faces turned down in Sky, the blades left as outlines, a turning propeller's blur, the wing roundels blue and red and the fuselage's blue, white and red (Sky on the undersides throughout, though before June 1940 they were black and white, and the fuselage roundel's yellow ring left out)
\ the Spitfire's aerial mast behind the hood, a tapered outline; the Hurricane's mast and its wire to the fin
: spitfire-mast ( -- points ) [ [ 0 0.57 -0.68 ] [ 0 1.22 -0.77 ] [ 0 1.22 -0.83 ] [ 0 0.57 -0.86 ] ] ;
: hurricane-mast ( -- points ) [ [ 0 0.68 -1.9 ] [ 0 1.48 -1.9 ] [ 0 1.37 -5.5 ] ] ;

\ the Spitfire's fuselage rings from the cowling to the tail, the seventh the first behind the hood
: spitfire-rings ( -- rings )
	[ [ 3.42 0.33 0.36 -0.03 ] [ 3.0 0.41 0.49 -0.13 ] [ 2.2 0.42 0.58 -0.19 ] [ 1.3 0.42 0.60 -0.20 ] [ 0.6 0.43 0.61 -0.20 ]
	  [ -0.10 0.40 0.55 -0.25 ] [ -0.12 0.33 0.695 -0.105 ] [ -1.4 0.34 0.64 -0.09 ] [ -2.6 0.25 0.52 -0.08 ]
	  [ -4.6 0.085 0.33 0 ] [ -5.0 0.04 0.25 0 ] ] ;

\ the fighters' code letters in Medium Sea Grey, the serial in black (estimates of the shades)
0xa0a4a2 constant code-letter-colour
0x161616 constant serial-colour

\ a point on a side of a body of rings of a number of sides about the line through the origin, -1 the left and 1 the right, at a station along and a height: on the face of the ring between the two corners the height falls between, a distance proud of it across
: ring-side-point ( rings n-sides along up side proud -- point )
	| rings n-sides along up side proud |
	rings along body-ring-at spread to lift to half-height to half-width drop
	half-width to across
	0 n-sides 2 / 1 do k
		k n-sides / TAU * to upper-angle
		k 1+ n-sides / TAU * to lower-angle
		upper-angle cos half-height * lift + to upper-height
		lower-angle cos half-height * lift + to lower-height
		up upper-height <= up lower-height >= and if
			up upper-height - lower-height upper-height - / to share
			upper-angle sin lower-angle sin upper-angle sin - share * + half-width * to across
		then
	loop
	[ side across proud + * up along ] ;

\ lettering painted on a side of a body of rings of a number of sides, -1 the left and 1 the right: each character's strokes from the stroke font as bands 0.8 of a grid unit wide, a grid unit a sixth of the capital height, on the skin a little proud of it, the capitals a height tall about a height up; read from the nose toward the tail on the left side and from the tail toward the nose on the right, so it reads left to right either way, the first character's leading edge at a station along
: sketch-body-lettering ( sketch rings n-sides text start height up side colour -- )
	| sketch rings n-sides text start height up side colour |
	height 6 / to unit
	unit 0.8 * 2 / to half-band
	up height 2 / + to top
	( place | rings n-sides place first place second side 0.03 ring-side-point ) to on-skin
	text upper-case string>chars to characters
	0 characters size 1 do k
		stroke-glyphs characters k @i string>symbol null @or to strokes
		strokes null? not if
			strokes ( stroke |
				0 stroke size 2 - 2 do p
					start k 5 * stroke p @i + unit * side * + to a0
					top stroke p 1+ @i unit * - to u0
					start k 5 * stroke p 2 + @i + unit * side * + to a1
					top stroke p 3 + @i unit * - to u1
					a1 a0 - to da
					u1 u0 - to du
					da sq du sq + sqrt half-band / to scale
					du negate scale / to na
					da scale / to nu
					[ [ a0 na + u0 nu + ] [ a1 na + u1 nu + ] [ a1 na - u1 nu - ] [ a0 na - u0 nu - ] ]
					on-skin map to corners
					sketch corners [ 0 up a0 a1 + 2 / ] colour sketch-painted-plate
				loop
			) each
		then
	loop ;

\ the code letters' height and their gap from the fuselage roundel's edge, the serial's height (estimates)
0.5 constant code-letter-height
0.15 constant code-letter-gap
0.2 constant serial-height

\ the length along of lettering at a capital height: five grid units a character, less the last one's gap
: lettering-length ( text height -- metres ) | text height | text size 5 * 1- height 6 / * ;

\ a fighter's squadron code, its own letter and its serial on both sides of a body of rings of a number of sides, about its fuselage roundel at a station along of a radius and a height up: the code ahead of the roundel on the left side and behind it on the right, the letter on the other side of it, as the squadrons painted them; the serial, unless empty, behind the code and the letter, its leading edge at a station along
: sketch-markings ( sketch rings n-sides roundel-along roundel-radius up code letter serial serial-along -- )
	| sketch rings n-sides roundel-along roundel-radius up code letter serial serial-along |
	roundel-along roundel-radius + code-letter-gap + to ahead
	roundel-along roundel-radius - code-letter-gap - to behind
	code code-letter-height lettering-length to code-length
	sketch rings n-sides code ahead code-length + code-letter-height up -1 code-letter-colour sketch-body-lettering
	sketch rings n-sides letter behind code-letter-height up -1 code-letter-colour sketch-body-lettering
	sketch rings n-sides code behind code-length - code-letter-height up 1 code-letter-colour sketch-body-lettering
	sketch rings n-sides letter ahead code-letter-height up 1 code-letter-colour sketch-body-lettering
	serial size 0 > if
		sketch rings n-sides serial serial-along serial-height up -1 serial-colour sketch-body-lettering
		sketch rings n-sides serial serial-along serial serial-height lettering-length - serial-height up 1 serial-colour sketch-body-lettering
	then ;

\ the Spitfire's fuselage roundel: its station along, its radii and its height (the radii in the proportion of a Type A1's inner three rings, the yellow outer ring left out)
-2.3 constant spitfire-fuselage-roundel-along
[ 0.38 0.27 0.11 ] constant spitfire-fuselage-roundel-radii
-0.085 constant spitfire-fuselage-roundel-up

\ a Spitfire's squadron code, its own letter and, unless empty, its serial near the tail
: sketch-spitfire-markings ( sketch code letter serial -- )
	| sketch code letter serial |
	sketch spitfire-rings 8 spitfire-fuselage-roundel-along spitfire-fuselage-roundel-radii first spitfire-fuselage-roundel-up
	code letter serial -4.05 sketch-markings ;

: spitfire-sketch ( wheels-down -- sketch )
	| wheels-down |
	new-model-sketch sky-paint-colour :under-colour ! to model
	model spitfire-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	model spitfire-spinner-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	[ 0 1 2 ] ( blade | model spitfire-hub blade 3 / TAU * 0.35 + spitfire-blade-widths propeller-blade sketch-loop ) each
	model spitfire-hub 1.64 sketch-propeller-disc
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		0 6 1 do stub
			3.15 stub 0.17 * - to along
			model [ [ side 0.42 * 0.12 along ] [ side 0.52 * 0.08 along 0.12 - ] ] sketch-path
		loop
	) each
	model sketch-hood
	model sketch-spitfire-wings
	model sketch-radiator
	model [ [ 1.375 0.11 0.11 0 ] [ 0.825 0.11 0.08 0.03 ] ] [ -1.4 -1.4 wing-underside-at 0.11 - 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	[ 0.15 0.6 1.0 1.3 1.5 1.58 ] to tail-stations
	tail-stations 1.6 1.15 -4.35 0.35 elliptical-outline to tailplane
	[ 0.15 0.8 1.5 ] 1.6 1.15 -4.35 0.35 0.3 elliptical-hinge to elevator
	model tailplane [ elevator ] 0 0.15 sketch-surface
	model 0 [ [ -3.55 0.14 ] [ -3.85 0.58 ] [ -4.15 0.94 ] [ -4.45 1.18 ] [ -4.75 1.25 ] [ -4.98 1.12 ] [ -5.1 0.76 ]
	          [ -5.12 0.27 ] [ -5.04 -0.22 ] [ -4.85 -0.35 ] [ -4.6 -0.31 ] ] [ [ -4.68 1.25 ] [ -4.68 -0.33 ] ] sketch-fin
	model spitfire-mast null sketch-plate
	model spitfire-dark-earth 0.45 spitfire-half-span ' spitfire-skin sketch-dark-earth
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		side 3.7 * to out
		[ out out wing-height-at 0.02 + out wing-leading-at out wing-trailing-at + 2 / ] to centre
		[ 1 side spitfire-dihedral * 0 ] v-unit to along-span
		[ side spitfire-dihedral * negate 1 0 ] v-unit to off-wing
		model centre along-span [ 0 0 1 ] off-wing [ spitfire-roundel-radius spitfire-roundel-centre-radius ] [ roundel-blue-colour roundel-red-colour ] sketch-roundel
		model [ side 0.28 * spitfire-fuselage-roundel-up spitfire-fuselage-roundel-along ] [ 0 0 1 ] [ 0 1 0 ] [ side 0 0 ] spitfire-fuselage-roundel-radii [ roundel-blue-colour roundel-white-colour roundel-red-colour ] sketch-roundel
	) each
	wheels-down if model sketch-undercarriage then
	model ;

: spitfire-model ( wheels-down -- model ) spitfire-sketch dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ the Spitfire preserved at Kelvingrove, LA198 of 602 (City of Glasgow) Squadron, in the code it carried, RAI-G (warmemorialsonline.org.uk, warbirdregistry.org): wheels up, its markings painted
: kelvingrove-spitfire-model ( -- model )
	false spitfire-sketch to model
	model "RAI" "G" "LA198" sketch-spitfire-markings
	model dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ === the Hurricane ===

\ The Hurricane Mk I is built to its published span and length (12.19 m,
\ 9.55 m) and wing area (23.92 m²). Every other figure is an estimate from
\ drawings, the wing's from the plan view of the three-view drawing by
\ M. L. Watts (Wikimedia Commons, public domain): the flat centre section
\ 3.2 m across at a chord of 2.45 m; the outer panels' leading edge swept
\ back 0.4 m to the tip, nearly straight, and the taper on the trailing
\ edge, which comes forward 0.85 m, to about 1.2 m at broad rounded tips;
\ 3.5° of dihedral outboard;
\ the deep fuselage and the raised spine behind the hood; the radiator
\ under the fuselage; the tall fin and big rudder; the tailplane; the
\ wide-track undercarriage folding inward; the propeller's 1.64 m radius.

1.6 constant hurricane-centre-half-span
6.095 constant hurricane-half-span
2.45 constant hurricane-root-chord
1.25 constant hurricane-root-leading
-1.2 constant hurricane-root-trailing
0.4 constant hurricane-leading-sweep
0.85 constant hurricane-trailing-advance
-0.45 constant hurricane-wing-height
3.5 PI 180 / * tan constant hurricane-dihedral

\ how far out along an outer panel a distance out lies, 0 at the centre section's edge and 1 at the tip
: hurricane-panel-share ( out -- share )
	abs hurricane-centre-half-span - 0 max2 hurricane-half-span hurricane-centre-half-span - / ;

\ the leading edge's and the trailing edge's places along the fuselage at a distance out: straight across the centre section; beyond it the leading edge swept back a little and the trailing edge coming forward
: hurricane-leading-at ( out -- along ) hurricane-panel-share hurricane-leading-sweep * hurricane-root-leading swap - ;
: hurricane-trailing-at ( out -- along ) hurricane-panel-share hurricane-trailing-advance * hurricane-root-trailing + ;

\ the wing's height at a distance out: level across the centre section, rising at the dihedral beyond
: hurricane-height-at ( out -- up ) abs hurricane-centre-half-span - 0 max2 hurricane-dihedral * hurricane-wing-height + ;

\ the right wing's centre section and outer panel outlines, the outer flap's hinge and the aileron's, as [ out along ] points
: hurricane-centre-outline ( -- pairs )
	hurricane-centre-half-span to inner
	[ [ 0 hurricane-root-leading ] [ inner hurricane-root-leading ] [ inner hurricane-root-trailing ] [ 0 hurricane-root-trailing ] ] ;
: hurricane-outer-outline ( -- pairs )
	hurricane-centre-half-span to inner
	[ inner 2.5 3.5 4.5 5.3 5.8 ] ( out | [ out out hurricane-leading-at ] ) map
	[ [ 5.95 0.83 ] [ 6.05 0.67 ] [ 6.095 0.23 ] [ 6.05 -0.18 ] [ 5.95 -0.34 ] ] concat
	[ 5.8 5.0 4.0 3.0 inner ] ( out | [ out out hurricane-trailing-at ] ) map concat ;
\ the split flaps from 0.35 m out, under the fuselage's side, to the aileron, 9 ft 6 in a side, their chord from their total area, 25.11 sq ft, 0.40 m; the ailerons 7 ft 8½ in long, their chord behind the hinge from their area less the balance's, 10.2 and 2.92 sq ft, 0.29 m (Nissen and Phillips, NACA MR, April 1942); the aileron's ends where the Watts three-view puts them, 3.25 m and 5.54 m out
0.35 constant hurricane-flap-inner
3.25 constant hurricane-aileron-inner
5.54 constant hurricane-aileron-outer
0.40 constant hurricane-flap-chord
0.29 constant hurricane-aileron-chord
: hurricane-centre-flap-hinge ( -- pairs ) [ hurricane-flap-inner hurricane-centre-half-span ] ( out | [ out out hurricane-trailing-at hurricane-flap-chord + ] ) map ;
: hurricane-flap-hinge ( -- pairs ) [ hurricane-centre-half-span hurricane-aileron-inner ] ( out | [ out out hurricane-trailing-at hurricane-flap-chord + ] ) map ;
: hurricane-aileron-hinge ( -- pairs ) [ hurricane-aileron-inner 4.4 hurricane-aileron-outer ] ( out | [ out out hurricane-trailing-at hurricane-aileron-chord + ] ) map ;

\ the Clark YH section's upper surface over its flat underside, [ share of the chord back from the leading edge, share of the thickness ]
[ [ 0 0 ] [ 0.05 0.68 ] [ 0.15 0.94 ] [ 0.3 1.0 ] [ 0.5 0.885 ] [ 0.7 0.6 ] [ 0.9 0.24 ] [ 1 0 ] ] constant hurricane-rib-profile

\ the leading and trailing edges at a distance out: the straight edges to 5.8 m, then round the tip through the outline's points
: hurricane-edges-at ( out -- leading trailing )
	| out |
	out abs to distance
	distance 5.8 <= if distance hurricane-leading-at distance hurricane-trailing-at exit then
	[ 5.8 5.95 6.05 6.095 ] to stations
	stations [ 5.8 hurricane-leading-at 0.83 0.67 0.23 ] distance table-at
	stations [ 5.8 hurricane-trailing-at -0.34 -0.18 0.23 ] distance table-at ;

\ the wing's upper surface at a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge: the section's thickness, 19% of the chord through the centre section thinning to 12.2% at the tip (published), over the flat underside
: hurricane-upper-at ( out fraction -- up )
	| out fraction |
	out hurricane-edges-at - to chord
	out hurricane-panel-share 0.122 0.19 - * 0.19 + chord * to depth
	hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair first ) map hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair second ) map fraction table-at depth *
	out hurricane-height-at + ;

\ the point on the wing's upper surface a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge
: hurricane-skin ( out share -- point )
	| out share |
	out hurricane-edges-at to trailing to leading
	[ out out share hurricane-upper-at leading leading trailing - share * - ] ;

\ the wings: the centre section's outline and flaps level, the outer panels' outlines, flaps and ailerons at their dihedral, the tips rounded, all on the wing's flat underside; the cambered upper surface over it, a Clark YH section 19% of the chord thick through the centre section thinning to 12.2% at the tip (the published figures), drawn as ribs at five stations with the skin filled between them; the four gun ports in each wing's leading edge
: sketch-hurricane-wings ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	hurricane-centre-half-span to inner
	hurricane-centre-outline to centre-outline
	sketch centre-outline [ hurricane-centre-flap-hinge ] 0 hurricane-wing-height sketch-surface
	hurricane-outer-outline to outline
	inner hurricane-dihedral * hurricane-wing-height swap - to outer-height
	hurricane-flap-hinge to flap-hinge
	hurricane-aileron-hinge to aileron-hinge
	hurricane-aileron-inner to split
	[ flap-hinge aileron-hinge [ [ split split hurricane-trailing-at ] [ split split hurricane-trailing-at hurricane-flap-chord + ] ] ] to hinges
	sketch outline hinges hurricane-dihedral outer-height sketch-surface
	[ 0.55 1.6 3.0 4.5 5.6 ] ( out |
		out hurricane-leading-at to rib-leading
		rib-leading out hurricane-trailing-at - to rib-chord
		out hurricane-panel-share 0.122 0.19 - * 0.19 + rib-chord * to rib-depth
		out hurricane-height-at to rib-base
		[ rib-leading rib-chord rib-depth rib-base ]
	) map to ribs
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ 0.55 1.6 3.0 4.5 5.6 ] ribs ( out rib |
			rib spread to rib-base to rib-depth to rib-chord to rib-leading
			sketch hurricane-rib-profile
				( pair | [ out side * rib-base pair second rib-depth * + rib-leading pair first rib-chord * - ] ) map sketch-points
		) 2 nmap to rib-indices
		rib-indices ( indices | sketch indices join-path ) each
		0 rib-indices size 1- 1 do r
			rib-indices r @i to inner-rib
			rib-indices r 1+ @i to outer-rib
			0 inner-rib size 1- 1 do j
				[ inner-rib j @i inner-rib j 1+ @i outer-rib j 1+ @i outer-rib j @i ] to quad
				sketch quad sketch quad inside-of [ 0 0.3 0 ] v- sketch-face
			loop
		loop
	) each
	[ 2.2 2.4 2.6 2.8 ] ( out |
		[ -1 1 ] ( side |
			sketch [ [ out side * out hurricane-height-at out hurricane-leading-at ] [ out side * out hurricane-height-at out hurricane-leading-at 0.12 + ] ] sketch-path
		) each
	) each ;

\ the Hurricane's sliding hood's four frames, each an arch from sill to sill leaning back 0.09 m from its sill to its top, from front to rear
: hurricane-hood-frames ( -- frames )
	[ [ -0.34 0.46 ] [ -0.32 0.70 ] [ -0.17 0.83 ] [ 0.17 0.83 ] [ 0.32 0.70 ] [ 0.34 0.46 ] ] to arch
	[ 0.05 -0.25 -0.6 -0.95 ] ( along | arch ( point |
		[ point first point second along point second 0.46 - 0.37 / 0.09 * - 0.045 + ] ) map ) map ;

\ the hood: the windscreen raked straight back from its base to the hood's top, a triangle each side and its base across; the sliding hood's four frames, flat-sided with a bar across each side and a flat top, each leaning back 0.09 m from its sill to its top, joined along the sills, the bars and the top's corners; the solid fairing behind it is the fuselage's (heights and positions measured on the side and plan views of the Mk I three-view by M. L. Watts, scaled to the published 9.55 m length)
: sketch-hurricane-hood ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch [ [ side 0.30 * 0.55 0.38 ] [ side 0.17 * 0.83 0.06 ] [ side 0.33 * 0.46 0.12 ] ] sketch-loop
	) each
	sketch [ [ -0.30 0.55 0.38 ] [ 0.30 0.55 0.38 ] ] sketch-path
	hurricane-hood-frames to frames
	frames ( frame | sketch frame sketch-path ) each
	0 6 1 do corner
		sketch [ frames first corner @i frames last corner @i ] sketch-path
	loop ;

\ the undercarriage: each leg standing straight down from the centre section, the wheel on its inboard side for the published track of 7 ft 10 in, the leg's cover outboard of it, narrow at the wing, its front edge slanting far forward down to a long bottom edge just above the hub over the tyre's top, its rear edge dropping nearly straight and stepping back at the bottom; the tail wheel (the wheel's size and place and the leg's measured on the side and front views of the Mk I three-view by M. L. Watts; the door's shape from a photograph)
: sketch-hurricane-undercarriage ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		hurricane-mk-i-figures :main-wheel @ spread to wheel-along to wheel-up to wheel-out
		[ side wheel-out * wheel-up wheel-along ] to axle
		1.385 hurricane-height-at to wing
		sketch [ [ side 1.385 * wing wheel-along ] [ side 1.385 * wheel-up wheel-along ] axle ] sketch-path
		sketch [ [ side 1.40 * wing 0.82 ] [ side 1.40 * -1.56 1.52 ] [ side 1.40 * -1.56 0.435 ] [ side 1.40 * -1.17 0.70 ] [ side 1.40 * wing 0.59 ] ] null sketch-plate
		sketch axle [ side negate 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] hurricane-mk-i-figures :wheel-radius @ 0.26 0.35 sketch-wheel
	) each
	hurricane-mk-i-figures :tail-wheel @ to tail-wheel
	sketch [ [ 0 -0.70 -4.65 ] tail-wheel ] sketch-path
	sketch tail-wheel [ 0 0 1 ] [ 0 1 0 ] hurricane-mk-i-figures :tail-wheel-radius @ 8 ring-of tyre-colour sketch-plate ;

\ the Hurricane's tailplane, its right half as [ out along ] points, and its elevator's hinge; the fin and rudder as [ along up ] points, and the rudder's hinge
: hurricane-tailplane ( -- pairs )
	[ [ 0.15 -4.75 ] [ 0.8 -4.82 ] [ 1.3 -4.93 ] [ 1.6 -5.08 ] [ 1.68 -5.28 ] [ 1.58 -5.55 ] [ 1.0 -5.82 ] [ 0.15 -5.95 ] ] ;
: hurricane-elevator ( -- pairs ) [ [ 0.15 -5.45 ] [ 1.0 -5.42 ] [ 1.55 -5.4 ] ] ;
: hurricane-fin ( -- pairs )
	[ [ -4.35 0.25 ] [ -4.5 0.53 ] [ -4.7 0.81 ] [ -4.9 1.03 ] [ -5.1 1.2 ] [ -5.3 1.32 ] [ -5.5 1.37 ] [ -5.7 1.35 ] [ -5.9 1.24 ]
	  [ -6.1 0.92 ] [ -6.25 0.46 ] [ -6.2 0.0 ] [ -6.1 -0.33 ] [ -5.9 -0.43 ] [ -5.7 -0.49 ] [ -5.5 -0.5 ] ] ;
: hurricane-rudder ( -- pairs ) [ [ -5.5 1.37 ] [ -5.5 -0.5 ] ] ;

\ the Hurricane Mk I: the fuselage of ten-sided rings from the cowling to the rudder's hinge, deep to its end, and the keel along its underside from the tail wheel to the rudder's lower corner, the spinner and the three-blade propeller, six exhaust stubs a side, the hood and spine, the wings, the radiator under the fuselage, a tub with a U-shaped section deepest behind its intake, the tailplane and elevators, the fin and rudder, the aerial mast and its wire, the roundels on the upper wings, each tilted to its wing's dihedral, and on the fuselage's sides; the undercarriage when down. Filled as the Spitfire is, in Dark Green with its own Dark Earth patches, Sky below
\ the Hurricane's fuselage rings from the cowling to the rudder's hinge, the seventh the first behind the hood
: hurricane-rings ( -- rings )
	[ [ 2.85 0.28 0.285 0.035 ] [ 2.5 0.38 0.40 0 ] [ 2.1 0.51 0.55 -0.07 ] [ 1.5 0.55 0.635 -0.125 ] [ 0.5 0.53 0.69 -0.13 ]
	  [ -0.95 0.53 0.64 -0.18 ] [ -0.97 0.53 0.815 -0.005 ] [ -1.4 0.53 0.795 -0.015 ] [ -2.5 0.47 0.655 -0.105 ] [ -3.5 0.37 0.51 -0.16 ]
	  [ -4.5 0.25 0.49 -0.24 ] [ -5.3 0.12 0.33 -0.26 ] [ -5.5 0.08 0.30 -0.25 ] ] ;

\ the Hurricane's fuselage roundel, behind the hood: its station along, its radii and its height (estimates from photographs, the radii as the Spitfire's, a Type A1's inner three rings, the yellow outer ring left out)
-2.4 constant hurricane-fuselage-roundel-along
[ 0.38 0.27 0.11 ] constant hurricane-fuselage-roundel-radii
0.02 constant hurricane-fuselage-roundel-up

\ a roundel painted on each side of a body of rings of a number of sides: discs of sixteen points about a station along and a height up, each laid on the skin a little prouder than the one before, from the largest, a colour for each
: sketch-skin-roundel ( sketch rings n-sides along up radii colours -- )
	| sketch rings n-sides along up radii colours |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		0 radii size 1 do k
			radii k @i to radius
			0.03 k 0.006 * + to proud
			[ 0 16 1 do c
				c 16 / TAU * to angle
				rings n-sides along angle cos radius * + up angle sin radius * + side proud ring-side-point
			loop ] to corners
			sketch corners [ 0 up along ] colours k @i sketch-painted-plate
		loop
	) each ;

: hurricane-sketch ( wheels-down -- sketch )
	| wheels-down |
	new-model-sketch sky-paint-colour :under-colour ! to model
	model hurricane-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 10 sketch-body
	model hurricane-spinner-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	[ 0 1 2 ] ( blade | model hurricane-hub blade 3 / TAU * 0.35 + hurricane-blade-widths propeller-blade sketch-loop ) each
	model hurricane-hub 1.64 sketch-propeller-disc
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		0 6 1 do stub
			2.45 stub 0.2 * - to along
			model [ [ side 0.52 * 0.17 along ] [ side 0.62 * 0.13 along 0.12 - ] ] sketch-path
		loop
	) each
	model sketch-hurricane-hood
	model sketch-hurricane-wings
	model [ [ 0.10 0.465 0.14 -0.96 ] [ -0.05 0.465 0.18 -1.0 ] [ -0.3 0.465 0.20 -1.02 ] [ -0.6 0.465 0.19 -1.01 ]
	        [ -0.9 0.43 0.15 -0.97 ] [ -1.14 0.3 0.01 -0.83 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 10 sketch-body
	model [ [ 0 -0.73 -4.5 ] [ 0 -0.5 -5.5 ] ] sketch-path
	model hurricane-tailplane [ hurricane-elevator ] 0 0.15 sketch-surface
	model 0 hurricane-fin hurricane-rudder sketch-fin
	model hurricane-mast sketch-path
	model hurricane-dark-earth 0.55 6.095 ' hurricane-skin sketch-dark-earth
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		side 4.2 * to out
		[ out out 0.5 hurricane-upper-at 0.03 + out hurricane-leading-at out hurricane-trailing-at + 2 / ] to centre
		[ 1 side hurricane-dihedral * 0 ] v-unit to along-span
		[ side hurricane-dihedral * negate 1 0 ] v-unit to off-wing
		model centre along-span [ 0 0 1 ] off-wing [ hurricane-roundel-radius hurricane-roundel-centre-radius ] [ roundel-blue-colour roundel-red-colour ] sketch-roundel
	) each
	model hurricane-rings 10 hurricane-fuselage-roundel-along hurricane-fuselage-roundel-up hurricane-fuselage-roundel-radii
	[ roundel-blue-colour roundel-white-colour roundel-red-colour ] sketch-skin-roundel
	wheels-down if model sketch-hurricane-undercarriage then
	model ;

: hurricane-model ( wheels-down -- model ) hurricane-sketch dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ a Hurricane's squadron code and its own letter about its fuselage roundel
: sketch-hurricane-markings ( sketch code letter -- )
	| sketch code letter |
	sketch hurricane-rings 10 hurricane-fuselage-roundel-along hurricane-fuselage-roundel-radii first hurricane-fuselage-roundel-up
	code letter "" 0 sketch-markings ;

\ a fighter of a kind, :spitfire or :hurricane, wheels up or down, in a squadron's code and its own letter; the plain model where the code is empty
: marked-model ( kind code letter wheels-down -- model )
	| kind code letter wheels-down |
	kind :hurricane = if wheels-down hurricane-sketch else wheels-down spitfire-sketch then to model
	code size 0 > if
		kind :hurricane = if model code letter sketch-hurricane-markings else model code letter "" sketch-spitfire-markings then
	then
	model dark-green-colour sketch>object ;
